This is a fantastic project for learning web development! It combines layout skills (CSS), interactivity (JavaScript), and data management (HTML).

Here is a step-by-step tutorial to build your interactive School Campus Map.

### Prerequisites
*   A code editor (like **VS Code** or **Notepad++**).
*   A web browser (Chrome, Firefox, or Edge).
*   **One Image:** You need a map image of your campus. Let's name it `campus-map.png` and place it in a folder with your code.

---

### Step 1: Project Setup
1.  Create a new folder on your computer named `SchoolMap`.
2.  Inside that folder, create a file named `index.html`.
3.  Create a file named `style.css`.
4.  Create a file named `script.js`.
5.  Place your `campus-map.png` inside this folder.

---

### Step 2: The HTML Structure (`index.html`)
We need a container for the map and a container for the information panel on the right.

**Copy and paste this code into `index.html`:**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Interactive School Campus Map</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>

    <div class="main-container">
        <!-- Left Side: The Map -->
        <div class="map-container">
            <img src="campus-map.png" alt="School Campus Map" id="campus-map">

            <!-- We will add the clickable buildings here using JavaScript -->
            <div id="buildings-layer"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Right Side: The Info Panel -->
        <div class="info-panel">
            <h2 id="building-title">Select a Building</h2>
            <p id="building-desc">Click on a building on the map to view details.</p>
            <img id="building-img" src="" alt="Building Image" style="display:none; max-width:100%; border-radius: 5px;">
            <a id="building-link" href="#" target="_blank" style="display:none; margin-top:10px; color:blue;">View More Info</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

